        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Import and export figures come as European leaders prepare to meet this week to address growing imbalance</p><p>The EU’s trade deficit with China has reached a record €1bn (£0.8bn) a day, according to official trade data, fuelling concerns over the future of Europe’s “industrial backbone”.</p><p>The gap between the EU’s imports from China and exports to China amounted to €31.9bn in April, according to the latest import and export data from the EU statistics body Eurostat.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jun/15/eu-trade-deficit-with-china-record-1bn-a-day\">Continue reading...</a>"
